00:47:28.160 --> 00:47:38.450
Brendan Miller: And, I'm gonna simplify here. There's other kind of edge cases. Relationship credentials, these are the core credential, peer-to-peer credential between two people.

323
00:47:38.450 --> 00:47:41.690
Brendan Miller: Or two entities, I should say, really more likely.

324
00:47:41.690 --> 00:48:05.529
Brendan Miller: And the idea is that by default, these are pairwise private relationship DIDs, sometimes membership DIDs, that, allow you to, indicate, unidirectionally. So I indicate that I have a relationship with you, and you indicate you have a relationship with me. That's described in a little more detail here. We want to make sure these support zero-knowledge

